<title>BELGIUM: EU swine fever bans eased.</title>
<headline>EU swine fever bans eased.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Movement restrictions on pigs in Germany and the Netherlands were eased by the European Union's Standing Veterinary Committee on Tuesday, an EU Commission official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Restrictions preventing movement of pigs in five German states were eased to cover regions where outbreaks have occurred and their surrounding veterinary regions, the official said.</p>
<p>A movement restriction covering the Netherlands was eased to allow animals in the Rijsbergen region on the Belgian border to be slaughtered and sold.</p>
<p>&quot;The vets accepted that there has only been one outbreak in Rijsbergen and that it involved an imported animal,&quot; the official added.</p>
</text>
